```

The server starts on http://localhost:3000 in **dry-run mode** (no API keys needed). It logs every SMS/email it *would* send.

## Test the flow

1. Create a client:
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/clients \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name":"Acme Dental","review_link":"https://g.page/r/XXXX/review"}'
```

2. Post a completed job (scheduled 3h out):
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/jobs \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"client_id":1,"customer_name":"Jane","customer_phone":"+15551234567","customer_email":"jane@example.com","delay_hours":0}'
```

3. Watch the console — within 60 seconds the dry-run loop fires and logs the message.

## Going live

Fill in `.env`:
- `TWILIO_SID`, `TWILIO_TOKEN`, `TWILIO_FROM` — from twilio.com
- `RESEND_KEY`, `RESEND_FROM` — from resend.com (verify your domain first)

Restart the server. It will print `LIVE mode`.

## Deploy

Any $6/mo VPS (Hetzner, DigitalOcean, Fly.io). Run with `pm2 start server.js --name reviewpilot` or a systemd unit.

## Endpoints

- `GET /` — health check
- `POST /clients` — create a client
- `GET /clients` — list clients
- `POST /jobs` — schedule a review request
- `GET /jobs` — list recent jobs
